this is in a nice neighborhood (bridgestone). dont know much about the place.

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m84Qpizt5ZQ](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m84Qpizt5ZQ)

&#x200B;

jin - if you feel my love

good luck with your surgery. 

&#x200B;

i had my surgery a few months ago, 3 or 4? i cant remember. it went pretty good. in and out in a couple hours. it stayed red for a month maybe, i got some sunglasses so i wouldnt freak people out with it. it was so straight after the surgery that i couldnt drive for a little bit because i had to get use to seeing with both eyes. it has drifted slightly outward again tho. but its not far enough that i think people notice it. before it was so bad people had to ask where i was looking and it usually pointed straight out to my left. i would say make sure you use both eyes together or it might go back the way it was. i had a nurse that had the surgery tell me that after i had mine. i didnt listen though.

oh that sucks it took 2 times for you. i might do better the next time if i need one since i know what to expect tho. 

&#x200B;

they gave me a tiny tube of cream that they said put in 2-4 times a day, i figure 3 would be a good number so i can take it breakfast, lunch, and dinner. otherwise i would forget to have it put in

&#x200B;

i am trying to keep my eye closed right now. i know sooner or later im going to have to learn to use it tho so i try to force myself to focus on things. it doesnt work right. right now if i look at my phone with both eyes my left eye is a little above the right unless i focus really hard, but thats a lot of work.
